{"cuisine/cossack-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cossack-cuisine","n":"Cossack cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"Cuisine of a people","intro":[["Cossack cuisine is the traditional cuisine of the Cossack people of present-day Ukraine and Russia. Having emerged in parallel with the settlement of Eastern European steppes, Cossack food culture incorporated elements of various traditions, including European, Caucasian and Central Asian cuisines."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cossack_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]}],"cont":"European cuisine"},"cuisine/epirotic-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/epirotic-cuisine","n":"Epirotic cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]],"sub":"Regional cuisine in Greece","intro":[["Epirotic cuisine is the traditional Greek cuisine of the region of Epirus. It is based mostly on dairy products; butter and various cheeses."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"epirotic-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epirotic_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine"},"dish/argentine-pizza":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/argentine-pizza","n":"Argentine pizza","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Argentine cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Argentine pizza, also known as Porteño-style pizza, is a mainstay of the country's cuisine, especially of its capital Buenos Aires, where it is regarded as a cultural heritage and icon of the city. Argentina is the country with the most pizzerias per inhabitant in the world and, although they are consumed throughout the country, the highest concentration of pizzerias and customers is in Buenos Aires, the city with the highest consumption of pizzas in the world (estimated in 2015 to be 14 million per year). As such, the city has been considered one of the world capitals of pizza."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-argentine-pizza"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Argentine_pizza"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Argentine cuisine","cuisine/argentine-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Mozzarella","ingredient/mozzarella"],["Tomato sauce","ingredient/tomato-sauce"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Familia Kitchen: Argentina","ref":"site/familiakitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"familiakitchen.com","note":"Argentine recipes and stories on a Latino family cooking site.","url":"https://familiakitchen.com/destination/argentina/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Argentine cuisine","links":[["Anticucho","dish/anticucho"],["Asado","dish/asado"],["Bara brith","dish/bara-brith"],["Bondiola sandwich","dish/bondiola-sandwich"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Dulce de batata","dish/dulce-de-batata"],["Fugazza","dish/fugazza"],["Jesuita (sandwich)","dish/jesuita-sandwich"],["Jésuite","dish/jesuite"],["Matambre","dish/matambre"],["Ox (Portland restaurant)","dish/ox-portland-restaurant"],["Puchero","dish/puchero"],["Rogel (cake)","dish/rogel-cake"],["Salsa golf","dish/salsa-golf"]]}]},"dish/bobcat-bite":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/bobcat-bite","n":"Bobcat Bite","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Bobcat Bite is a restaurant that is located in Santa Fe, New Mexico, off of the Old Las Vegas Highway. The location itself has hosted two businesses, both of which have gone by the name \"Bobcat Bite\". The original Bobcat Bite specialized in the preparation of steak, chops, and hamburgers."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe