rlottes, and are also used as fruit or chocolate gateau linings, and for the sponge element of tiramisu. They are typically soaked in a sugar syrup or liqueur, or in espresso for tiramisu."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-ladyfinger-biscuit"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ladyfinger_(biscuit)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]],["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Tiramisu","dish/tiramisu"]]],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas",[["Mango float","dish/mango-float"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Savoiarde PAT","ingredient/savoiarde-pat"],["Carabao mango","ingredient/carabao-mango"],["Condensed milk","ingredient/condensed-milk"],["Cracker","ingredient/cracker"],["Graham crackers","ingredient/graham-crackers"],["Mango","ingredient/mango"],["Whipped cream","ingredient/whipped-cream"],["Cocoa powder","ingredient/cocoa-powder"],["Coffee","ingredient/coffee"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Egg yolk","ingredient/egg-yolk"],["Espresso","ingredient/espresso"],["Marsala wine","ingredient/marsala-wine"],["Mascarpone","ingredient/mascarpone"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]}]},"ingredient/minced-beef":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/minced-beef","n":"Minced beef","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Ground beef, hamburger meat (North American English), minced beef or beef mince (Commonwealth English; often just generically referred to as mince or mincemeat) is beef that has been finely chopped with a knife or meat grinder (North American), i.e., mincer or mincing machine (Commonwealth). It is used in many recipes including hamburgers, bolognese sauce, meatloaf, meatballs, kofta, and burritos."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-minced-beef"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minced_beef"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Scottish cuisine","cuisine/scottish-cuisine",[["Mince and tatties","dish/mince-and-tatties"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Mashed potatoes","ingredient/mashed-potatoes"]]}]},"dish/rainbow-roll":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/rainbow-roll","n":"Rainbow roll","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Rainbow roll is a type of uramaki sushi roll filled with cucumber, avocado and crab stick. It is prepared with multiple types of fish, most commonly tuna, salmon, white fish, yellowtail, snapper, and eel. Rainbow roll is quite similar to the California roll, with the addition of tuna, salmon and avocado. Other variants include slices of mango next to avocado, or uses of imitation crab meat, fried shrimp tempura, and other seafood."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-rainbow-roll"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow_roll"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Avocado","ingredient/avocado"],["Crab stick","ingredient/crab-stick"],["Cucumber","ingredient/cucumber"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":true},{"name":"RecipeTin Japan","ref":"site/japan-recipetineats-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"japan.recipetineats.com","note":"Japanese home recipes from Yumiko, a Japan-born cook, sister site to RecipeTin Eats.","url":"https://japan.recipetineats.com/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Japanese cuisine","lin